## Unit (Vitest)
- Arrange/Act/Assert; cover happy path + edge cases (empty, nullish, boundary values).
- Avoid network & time dependence; mock/stub IO; keep tests < 200ms each when possible.

### Systematic test design (80/20)

- Clarify the behavior and **most important risks** first.
- Start with tests that cover:
  - The main happy path.
  - The most likely failure modes.
  - Critical a11y or perf constraints.
- Add additional cases when they materially improve confidence; avoid over‑specifying implementation details.

## Component tests
- Use @testing-library/react selectors by role/text; assert accessible behavior.

## E2E (Playwright)
- Test core flows only (smoke + auth + publish/view); use stable selectors (data-testids).
- Record traces/screenshots on failure; keep suites parallelizable.

## Quality gates
- Require CI to run lint, typecheck, unit, e2e smoke on PRs.
- Use `.cursor/commands/write-tests.md` for authoring workflow guidance and `.cursor/commands/review-code.md` for final QA passes.
- See `.cursor/rules/03-ci-cd.mdc` for the canonical CI pipeline and thresholds.
